{
  "definition": "Each family pairs its base arm (the reference) with its trained arm over the same scenarios and decoder draws, from each arm's accepted bundle outcomes. A bundle holds one full-ruleset judgment F and one separate-call judgment R_k per rule; its aggregate A is the largest R_k under no < unsure < yes. Every label is yes, unsure or no, and a bundle whose stored max_rule_phi or contradiction is not its labels' is refused. Each number is a mean over scenarios of a per-scenario value, or (by_anchor) a ratio of two such means. A rate between two sets of labels averages, per scenario, over all D x D pairs of a draw of one with a draw of the other; a rate within one arm's labels, over the D(D-1) ordered pairs of two different draws of it: exact averages over the draws at hand, each estimating the rate between independent temperature-1 draws (an arm's F against its own A counts the pairs within one bundle too, which estimate the same rate because each call of a bundle is sampled on a seed of its own). Inconsistency rates, the share of pairs in which F differs from A: base, the base arm's F against its own A, which are the frozen anchors; trained_updated, the trained arm's F against its own A; trained_frozen, the trained arm's F against the base arm's A. differences: base minus trained_frozen (the reduction left when evaluation keeps the frozen anchors), base minus trained_updated, trained_frozen minus trained_updated, and trained_frozen minus always_yes, an always-yes judge's rate against the frozen anchors (the base arm's always_yes), which trained_frozen compares with directly. by_anchor: base and trained_frozen again over only the pairs whose frozen anchor is yes, or is not yes: the share of those pairs in which F differs from A (undefined in a resample that holds none), with share, those pairs' share of all pairs, and base minus trained_frozen. same_draw: each arm's F against its own A at the same draw, averaged over draws, which is its root's own flat rate (its interval is this golden's bootstrap's, not the root's). Change rates, the share of pairs whose labels differ, for the individual-rule judgments (R_k paired by rule, averaged over the rules), the aggregate A and the full-ruleset judgment F: base_to_trained, the base arm's labels against the trained arm's; draw_to_draw, each arm's labels against its own at a different draw; resampling, the mean of the two arms' draw_to_draw; excess, base_to_trained minus resampling, whose expectation for one scenario is half the squared distance between the two arms' label distributions: the part of the change that is a shift in the judgment's distribution, not resampling (a per-scenario value may be negative). label_shares: the share of each arm's bundles whose F, or whose A, is each label. always_yes: an always-yes judge's inconsistency rate against each arm's aggregate, the share of its bundles whose A is not yes. Intervals: one scenario-cluster bootstrap per family over all its per-scenario values, at the reference root's bootstrap settings (bootstrap), so that every difference's interval is paired; percentile intervals, no tests.",
